      "body": "> skipping certificate checks is the whole point here. When that setting is off the default path should also be good already, no?\r\n\r\nYou're right — I re-checked: with the setting off, the connection already uses the platform socket factory and hostname verifier, and the trust-all context is only applied when the user opts in. The analysis flagged it because the context is built in the constructor regardless of the setting, but that isn't a problem in the default path. I'll close this; sorry for the noise.",
